title: The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> breaks with Askew
new-page: true
subtitle: The rise of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #003755;">opposition</span> has forced them to act.
tags: event
view-if: total_bruning_time >= 6 and marcher_toleration_right and dnf_votes + royalist_votes + traditionalist_angry >= (traditionalist_votes * 3) and bruning_time >= 3 and not concord_formed
on-arrival: pro_republic -= traditionalist_votes / 2; dufour_angry_bruning += 25; moderate_traditionalist_gallax = 1; gold_right += 3; lvp_right += 3; ddp_right += 1
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/dnvp4.jpg

= The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> breaks with Askew

The sharp rise of the <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> in local elections has triggered mass panic within the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, as pessimism and a noticeable shift away from democracy rapidly take hold within the once-constructive "democratic" party. They now believe that only closer cooperation with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #003755;">opposition</span> and a rightward shift in alignment with the nation can salvage their declining poll numbers.

Their first step toward this goal is an attempt to bring down the Askew government with the assistance of the anti-democratic parties, hoping either to force Askew into reorganizing his cabinet or to trigger elections that could deliver a right-wing majority. However, Mallin and Gallax remain committed to their all-or-nothing strategy, demanding the chancellorship outright from Askew. This leaves only the prospect of fresh elections as a possibility, with Gallax being very vague about what his government would look like. Given that Mallin and Gallax are far from the most trustworthy figures, the party remains in limbo for now.

Hopefully [+ traditionalist_leader +] can restore order within his party, and prevent new elections from delivering catastrophic gains for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #003755;">right</span>.

- @vonc_yes
- @vonc_no

@vonc_yes
title: Support the vote of no confidence, voting against the government.
subtitle: We will be the one to destroy Askew, screw you.
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_center_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; gold_relation -= 4; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 2; lvp_relation -= 3; reformist_dissent += 5
call: set_next_election_time
go-to: new_prussia_election if (in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland)

We have seized the initiative from the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, toppling Chancellor [+ chancellor +] government with the support of votes from the extremes of Commonwealth politics.

The <span style="color: #000000;">propertied</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> coalition has fallen. New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@vonc_no
title: Oppose the vote of no confidence, voting in favor of the government.
subtitle: We will hope that the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> manages to get its house in order.
on-arrival: left_dissent += 5
go-to: vonc_hergt if traditionalist_leader == "Hargen"; vonc_treviranus if traditionalist_leader == "Trevannon"; vonc_lambach if traditionalist_leader == "Maine"; vonc_moderate if traditionalist_leader == "Tilford" or traditionalist_leader == "Westmore"


@vonc_hergt
on-arrival: traditionalist_leader = "Westmore"

Cuthbert Hargen, who was once forced to resign nearly a decade ago over his decision to allow a free vote on the recovery accord—the very plan that rescued the Commonwealth from hyperinflation and ushered in the <span style="color: #FFDF00;">Golden Twenties</span>—is now tendering his resignation once again after failing to impose party discipline.

History seems to be repeating itself: the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> is once again deeply divided, with its pragmatic wing supporting Askew while its emboldened right wing aligns with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #003755;">opposition</span>. The party now faces a fateful decision—either accept the bitter pill of working within the system or risk catastrophic consequences, possibly even the destruction of the Unity Republic itself.

- @results: The Assembly convenes.

@results
on-arrival: {!
Q.pro_bruning_traditionalist = (Q.traditionalist_r * Q.reichstag_size) * Q.pro_republic / 100
Q.pro_bruning_traditionalist = Math.round(Q.pro_bruning_traditionalist)
Q.anti_bruning_traditionalist = (Q.traditionalist_r * Q.reichstag_size) - Q.pro_bruning_traditionalist
Q.anti_bruning_traditionalist = Math.round(Q.anti_bruning_traditionalist)

if (Q.pro_bruning_traditionalist >= Q.anti_bruning_traditionalist) {
Q.burgher_traditionalist -= 2;
Q.guild_traditionalist -= 4;
Q.landed_traditionalist -= 2; 
Q.burgher_dnf += 2;
Q.guild_dnf += 4;
Q.landed_dnf += 2; 
Q.pro_republic += 5;
Q.gold_left += 3;
Q.ddp_left += 1;
Q.lvp_left += 3;
} else if (Q.anti_bruning_traditionalist >= Q.pro_bruning_traditionalist) {
Q.burgher_traditionalist -= 4;
Q.guild_traditionalist += 2;
Q.landed_traditionalist += 2; 
Q.burgher_gold += 4;
Q.guild_dnf -= 2;
Q.landed_dnf -= 2; 
Q.gold_right += 3;
Q.ddp_right += 1;
Q.lvp_right += 3;
Q.time_to_election = 3;
Q.marcher_in_government = 0;
Q.in_right_coalition = 0;
}
!}
go-to: election_set if anti_bruning_traditionalist >= pro_bruning_traditionalist

Pro-Askew delegates: [+ pro_bruning_traditionalist +]

Anti-Askew delegates: [+ anti_bruning_traditionalist +]

[? if pro_bruning_traditionalist >= anti_bruning_traditionalist: The pro-Askew delegates have maintained control of the party, and the new leader of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, coincidentally Westmore again, has enforced party discipline, with only a few radical members voting against. ?][? if anti_bruning_traditionalist >= pro_bruning_traditionalist: The pro-Askew delegates have lost control of the party, and the majority of the party's delegation has agreed to back a vote of no confidence against Askew. Following Hargen's resignation, Westmore is, coincidentally, re-elected again shortly after. ?]

@vonc_treviranus
on-arrival: {!
Q.dnf_r += Q.traditionalist_r*0.2;
Q.traditionalist_r *= 0.8;
if (Q.kvp_formed && Q.lvp_formed) {
    Q.cordon_sanitaire = parseFloat((Q.marcher_r + Q.lvp_r + Q.unionist_r + Q.other_r + Q.kvp_r).toFixed(1));
} else if (Q.kvp_formed && !Q.lvp_formed) {
    Q.cordon_sanitaire = parseFloat((Q.marcher_r + Q.ddp_r + Q.unionist_r + Q.gold_r + Q.other_r + Q.traditionalist_r + Q.kvp_r).toFixed(1));
} else if (Q.lvp_formed && !Q.kvp_formed) {
    Q.cordon_sanitaire = parseFloat((Q.marcher_r + Q.unionist_r + Q.lvp_r + Q.other_r + Q.traditionalist_r).toFixed(1));
} else {
    Q.cordon_sanitaire = parseFloat((Q.marcher_r + Q.unionist_r + Q.ddp_r + Q.gold_r + Q.other_r + Q.traditionalist_r).toFixed(1));
}
Q.bruning_coalition = Q.cordon_sanitaire;
Q.bruning_coalition = Math.round((Q.bruning_coalition - Q.bruning_coalition_loss) * 10) / 10;
!}

Godwin Trevannon, a strong supporter of Askew and, to some extent, democracy, has enforced party discipline to ensure the Assembly delegation votes in favor of Askew. However, despite his efforts to democratize the party, many defy his orders and vote against Askew's government.

- @results2: The Assembly convenes.
- @results3: The Assembly convenes.

@results2
view-if: bruning_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: burgher_traditionalist -= 2; burgher_dnf += 2; burgher_royalist += 2; guild_traditionalist -= 4; guild_dnf += 2; guild_royalist += 4; landed_traditionalist -= 3; landed_royalist += 3; commons_traditionalist -= 2; commons_royalist += 2; gold_left += 1; ddp_left += 1; lvp_left += 1

Despite the defections of some members of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s parliamentary delegation to the <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span>, Askew's government has retained the support of [+ bruning_coalition +]% of the Assembly. However, despite this victory, the episode has severely radicalized the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s voters, leading many to defect to the more radical <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> and even the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>.

