Caradoc Maine, a strong supporter of Askew and, to some extent, democracy, has enforced party discipline to ensure the Assembly delegation votes in favor of Askew. However, the anger many within his party has against him and his <span style="color: #6D5298;">Faithful Social</span> ideals has split the party almost down the middle.

- @results6: The Assembly convenes.
- @results7: The Assembly convenes.

@results6
view-if: bruning_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: burgher_traditionalist -= 6; burgher_dnf += 4; burgher_royalist += 2; guild_traditionalist *= 0.5; guild_dnf += 4; guild_royalist += 2; landed_traditionalist *= 0.6; landed_dnf += 4; landed_royalist += 2; commons_traditionalist -= 2; commons_royalist += 2; gold_left += 1; ddp_left += 1; lvp_left += 1; lambachover = 1

Despite the defection of a significant portion of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s parliamentary delegation to the <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span>, Askew's government has retained the support of [+ bruning_coalition +]% of the Assembly. 

However, while this may seem like a victory, the loss of nearly 40% of the party's parliamentary group has triggered a broader defection of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s non-worker voter base to the <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span>—and even the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>.

@results7
view-if: bruning_coalition < 50
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; burgher_traditionalist -= 6; burgher_dnf += 4; burgher_royalist += 2; guild_traditionalist *= 0.5; guild_dnf += 4; guild_royalist += 2; landed_traditionalist *= 0.6; landed_dnf += 4; landed_royalist += 2; commons_traditionalist -= 2; commons_royalist += 2; lambachover = 1; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 1; lvp_right += 2
go-to: election_set

The defections of some members of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s parliamentary delegation to Mallin's <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> has successfully caused Askew to lose the vote of no confidence, ushering in new elections where the extremists stand to gain.

The loss of nearly 40% of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s parliamentary group has triggered a broader defection of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>'s non-worker voter base to the <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span>—and even the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>.

