[? if traditionalist_leader == "Tilford": Martin Tilford, a strong supporter of Askew—and his Minister of Agriculture—has successfully persuaded the <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> wing of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> to oppose the vote of confidence. He also enlists the support of Westmore and incumbent cabinet members to lobby the rest of the party. However, some radical members, who remained in the party solely due to their shared hatred of Mallin, are expected to defy party discipline. ?][? if traditionalist_leader == "Westmore": Kuno Westmore, a longtime leader of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and one of Askew's strongest supporters, has rallied members from all wings of the party to oppose the proposed vote of no confidence, warning of the political and economic instability that would follow if it passed. However, some radical members, who remained in the party solely due to their shared hatred of Mallin, are expected to defy party discipline. ?]

